'''Arvel Skeen''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who served under [[Vel Sartha]] as a part of her [[Aldhani rebel infiltration team|team]]. He was among the group who carried out a [[Aldhani heist|mission]] on the [[planet]] [[Aldhani]]. He was killed by [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] following the heist for his proposal to betray surviving members of the team.

==Biography==
{{Quote|The axe forgets, but the tree remembers.|Arvel Skeen, to Cassian Andor|<ref name="The Axe Forgets">{{Andor|The Axe Forgets}}</ref>}}
Skeen claimed to have had a brother that had been driven to suicide by the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]]. He was incarcerated at least twice, and received three tattoos, two of them being the [[Krayt Head]], along with the prison number 72742647, and [[By The Hand]], with the prison number 7424273 783836766.<ref name="The Axe Forgets" /><ref name="Andor Trivia">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e5-trivia-gallery|text="The Axe Forgets" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 6}}</ref>

By [[5 BBY]] Arvel Skeen was recruited for an operation on the planet [[Aldhani]], where the payroll for the entire [[sector]] was stored in a vault on the [[planet]]'s [[Galactic Empire]] [[Aldhani dam|headquarters]]. To that end, Skeen joined a six men [[Aldhani rebel infiltration team|infiltration team]] led by the [[Chandrilan]] [[Vel Sartha]]. The team which made [[Vel Sartha's camp|temporary camp]] on Aldhani highlands near the dam, where they were to train for the heist for the following [[Standard month|months]].<ref name="Aldhani" />

When Vel Sartha returned to camp with another recruit, whom she identified as [[Cassian Jeron Andor|"Clem,"]] Skeen did not approve of taking on another team member just three [[Standard day|days]] before the operation. His opinion was sternly dismissed by Sartha. When [[Gorn]], an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Lieutenant]] at the [[Aldhani Garrison]] and the inside man of their operation, traveled to camp, Skeen went to meet him and told him of the new development, which similarly annoyed Gorn. Sartha rejected their concerns and called a meeting, introducing their plan to Andor. When Andor questioned the plan, saying that it was a suicide run, Skeen commented that they were confident in the plan and that nobody was crazy enough to try it but them.<ref name="Aldhani" />

The following morning, Skeen went through the items Clem had brought with him, per Sartha's orders. This, along with Clem's injured arm, led Skeen to conclude that the newcomer had left his previous place in a hurry. He also took a special interest in the [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|corporate]]-issued blaster he found, questioning Clem about its previous owner. Noticing that Clem was eyeing his Krayt Head tattoo, Skeen understood the other man recognized its meaning. Then he asked Clem if he recognized the symbol on his right forearm, which he also did. The two briefly bonded over having been imprisoned in the past, until Clem questioned Skeen being motivated by revenge and expressed doubts about the team's likelihood of pulling off the plan. Skeen then shared his impressions on both [[Karis Nemik]] and [[Cinta Kaz]]<ref name="The Axe Forgets" />

Following the successful [[Aldhani heist|heist]], the surviving members of the team made a stop on the [[moon]] [[Frezno]] to visit [[Doctor|Dr.]] [[Quadpaw]] in hopes of saving [[Karis Nemik]]'s life. While he and Andor waited for the procedure to end, Skeen suggested that they abandon their teammates and flee with the haul, splitting the [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] fifty-fifty. As Skeen pressed on, Andor, now aware of his disloyalty, shot Skeen with his [[MW-20 Bryar pistol]] out of self-preservation, [[Death|killing]] him. When Andor confronted Sartha and Quadpaw in hopes of finding an escape, he informed them of Skeen's [[Treason|treachery]] and death after Sartha had called out for him.<ref name="The Eye">{{Andor|The Eye}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Arvel Skeen was played by [[Ebon Moss-Bachrach]] in the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''.<ref name="Aldhani" /> Aldhani was said to be Skeen's homeworld in [[2023 Topps Star Wars|2023 ''Topps Star Wars]],<ref name="2023 Topps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars|cardname=Arvel Skeen|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/370777/cid/22170387/2023-Topps-Star-Wars-57-Arvel-Skeen}}</ref> but [[Pablo Hidalgo]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] stated this was not the case.<ref name="Pablo Twitter">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1693067125491912721|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2023-08-19|quote=They're not. I doubt they'd call it home either. It sounds like a poor choice of description of a planet they happen to be associated with. {{C|In response to: Hey @pabl0hidalgo @missingwords, in the spirit of recent card game discussion, topps recently dropped a new set but I think these homeworlds don't add up? I guess it's not impossible but I never got a sense all were from aldhani}}|archivedate=20230820012834}}</ref>

